TAILS_OLD = r'''(iii) the $\overline{\rm MS}$ convolution $\int\frac{dy}{|y|}C(\frac xy)f(y)$ converges iff $\int_0|f(y)|dy<\infty$, the ratio/hybrid convolutions need only $\int_0|yf(y)|dy<\infty$; valence distributions satisfy both, Regge-like singlet sea/gluon distributions $y^{-1-\delta}$ ($\delta\ge0$) make the $\overline{\rm MS}$ momentum-space formula ill-defined. `% VF-LAM-9`'''
TAILS_NEW = r'''(iii) near $y=0$ the integrand of $\int\frac{dy}{|y|}C(\frac xy)f(y)$ is $-\frac{3a}{2|x|}f(y)(1+O(y))$ for $\overline{\rm MS}$, $\frac{3a}{2|x|}\big[\frac2\pi{\rm Si}(|x|z_SP^z)-1\big]f(y)(1+O(y))$ for the hybrid scheme (whose parameter is $\lambda_S=z_S|y|P^z$, so the decay of its bracket at fixed $\lambda_S$ does not help as $y\to0$), and $O(|yf(y)|)$ for the ratio scheme; hence $\overline{\rm MS}$ and hybrid converge absolutely iff $\int_{|y|<\epsilon}|f|<\infty$, the ratio scheme needs only $\int|yf|<\infty$; for physical quark distributions (antiquarks at $y<0$) the $O(1)$ terms combine into $q-\bar q$, so all three schemes give finite quark quasi-PDFs whenever $q-\bar q$ and $y(q+\bar q)$ are integrable at small $y$ — including a Regge-like sea $y^{-1-\delta}$ with $\delta<1$ (gluon kernels are not covered). `% VF-LAM-9`'''
TAILS_PEND_OLD = r'''  - *Pending.* Candidate 「本书新结果」 (planning marker only; claim N09) **[PENDING-VERIFY]**; until the patch, print as 「本书给出的推导」.'''
